\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Architecture of \texttt {metasignal}.} Trial-level stimulus, response, confidence, and rating-scale arrays (\texttt  {stim}, \texttt  {resp}, \texttt  {conf}, \texttt  {n\_ratings}) enter the stable \texttt  {stdpy} core, which computes Type-1 SDT quantities ($d'$, criterion $c$) and all 17 metacognitive measures; \texttt  {compute\_all\_measures} packages these into a single 26-element array (20 measures plus 6 meta-$d'$ fit diagnostics). This output feeds the \texttt  {analysis} layer (bootstrap confidence intervals, permutation tests, group summaries) and the \texttt  {metasignal compute} command-line interface, which accepts CSV input without requiring code. The dashed box shows optional, dependency-isolated extensions: \texttt  {sdtbayes} for hierarchical Bayesian estimation (seven modeling approaches) and \texttt  {itmc} for information-theoretic metacognition measures.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
